    <ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>&lt;div&gt;The following executive summary is available:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 1 June 2009, the Minister of Veterans Affairs introduced Bill C-33, An Act to amend the War Veterans Allowance Act, in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-33 amends the War Veterans Allowance Act to allow low-income Allied Veterans who moved to Canada after 1995 and resided in Canada for a total period of at least 10 years to apply for benefits.  It also proposes that eligibility be expanded to include Allied Veterans of the Korean War. Family members may also receive benefits.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>
    <ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>&lt;div&gt;Le résumé suivant est à votre disposition :&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le 1 juin 2009, le ministre des Anciens combattants a déposé le projet de loi C-33, Loi sur les allocations aux anciens combattants, à la Chambre des communes en première lecture.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Projet de loi C-33 vise a modifié la Loi sur les allocations aux anciens combattants pour permettre le droit aux avantages aux anciens combattants alliés de la Seconde Guerre mondiale à faible revenu qui s'étaient établis en Canada après 1995 et qui a résidé au Canada pendant une période globale d'au moins dix ans.  En plus, le projet de loi C-33 vise à inclure les anciens combattants alliés de la guerre de Corée afin d'offrir des avantages, et les familles de ces derniers.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>
    <ShortLegislativeSummary>&lt;div&gt;The following executive summary is available:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 1 June 2009, the Minister of Veterans Affairs introduced Bill C-33, An Act to amend the War Veterans Allowance Act, in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-33 amends the War Veterans Allowance Act to allow low-income Allied Veterans who moved to Canada after 1995 and resided in Canada for a total period of at least 10 years to apply for benefits.  It also proposes that eligibility be expanded to include Allied Veterans of the Korean War. Family members may also receive benefits.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummary>
